      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are doing the right thing by being open and supportive of your child's curiosity. You can explain that gender is about how someone feels inside, which is different from what they look like or what society expects. Acknowledging that people experience gender in many ways is a fundamental part of a modern, inclusive understanding of human diversity. This open dialogue fosters a healthy environment where your child feels safe to explore their own identity.",
